    println!("The Euclidean distance between the two points is: {}", distance);
}
```

This function works by summing the squares of the differences between corresponding coordinates of the two points, then taking the square root of this sum. The result is the Euclidean distance between the two points. Note that this function assumes that both points have the same number of dimensions. If they do not, the function will panic.

